    },
    "body": "This sets `permissions: contents: read` on the CI workflow and adds `persist-credentials: false` to every `actions/checkout` step, so the token no longer stays in `.git/config` for later steps to read.\n\nNothing is exploitable today: on this repository the token is already read-only, and no job needs more than reading the repository (caches and artifacts use the runner's own token, and the one `git fetch` reads a public repository). The change puts least privilege in the workflow itself rather than in the repository settings, so it also holds in forks, where each owner sets the default.\n\nPinning actions by hash is left out, after #35754 and the discussion in #36512.\n\nThe same change for libsecp256k1 is bitcoin-core/secp256k1#1964.\n\nCloses #36512.\n",
